{"name":"Shaded Glen","hex":"#8e824a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shaded","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Being in the shade, not in direct light.","Having a slight colour added (of a diagram or picture) or being slightly darkened as if in the shade."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of shade"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shaded"},{"term":"glen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A secluded and narrow valley, especially one with a river running through it; a depression between hills; a dale."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shading","blocks":[{"text":"Shading refers to the depiction of depth perception in 3D models or illustrations by varying the level of darkness. Shading tries to approximate local behavior of light on the object's surface and is not to be confused with techniques of adding shadows, such as shadow mapping or shadow volumes, which fall under global behavior of light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Flatshading01.png/330px-Flatshading01.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shading"},{"title":"Glen","blocks":[{"text":"A glen is a valley, typically one that is long and bounded by gently sloped concave sides, unlike a ravine, which is deep and bounded by steep slopes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Glendun_-_geograph.org.uk_-_465779.jpg/330px-Glendun_-_geograph.org.uk_-_465779.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glen"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Gouraudshading01.png/500px-Gouraudshading01.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/